                <h2>为什么出海团队需要合规巡检SOP</h2>
<p>海外广告平台的合规政策更新频繁，Facebook、TikTok、Google等渠道的政策标准存在差异，且违规判定往往缺乏明确通知。多数团队的合规问题往往在账户被封或广告被拒后才被发现，此时已造成投放中断和预算浪费。</p>
<p>一份可执行的合规巡检SOP，能帮助团队在问题扩大前主动发现风险，而不是被动救火。</p>
<hr />
<h2>巡检前准备：明确责任人与频率</h2>
<p>在执行巡检前，团队需要先确认以下基础设置：</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>事项</th>
<th>建议做法</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>责任人</td>
<td>指定1名运营或风控人员作为巡检负责人</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>巡检频率</td>
<td>高风险期（政策更新后）每日一次；稳定期每周一次</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>记录工具</td>
<td>使用共享表格记录每次巡检结果与问题跟进状态</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>环节一：平台政策核查（4项检查）</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>⚠️ 这一环节是大多数团队最容易忽略的。</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>政策公告追踪</strong>：每周登录各广告平台官方政策页面，查看最近7天内是否有政策更新。Facebook的"Policy Updates"、TikTok的"Ads policies"、Google Ads的"Policy updates"都有RSS或邮件订阅功能。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>账户状态确认</strong>：登录广告后台，逐一检查所有活跃账户的健康状态标识，确认无未处理的政策违规警告。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>广告审核历史</strong>：导出最近14天的广告审核记录，标记所有"被拒"或"限制"的广告，分析被拒原因是否涉及同一类问题。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>新限制区域</strong>：若近期有市场扩张计划，提前核查目标国家或地区是否有特殊限制，例如某些国家对金融产品、健康声称有严格要求。</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：<br />
- [ ] 已订阅各平台政策更新通知<br />
- [ ] 本周无新增政策违规警告<br />
- [ ] 已分析被拒广告的共性原因</p>
<hr />
<h2>环节二：素材合规审查（5项检查）</h2>
<p>素材是违规高发区，建议在素材上线前和巡检时都做复核：</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>文案声称核查</strong>：广告文案中不得出现绝对化用语（如"最好""100%有效"），也不得包含未经证实的比较声称。某工具类App曾因文案中"最快速"的表述被Facebook判定为不当声称。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>版权与商标</strong>：图片、视频中使用的背景音乐、字体、人物肖像均需确认已获得授权。背景音乐要使用平台音乐库或已购买商用版权的曲目。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>年龄分级与内容</strong>：确保素材内容符合目标市场的年龄分级要求，例如欧洲市场对酒精类广告有严格的年龄限制标识要求。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>前后对比声明</strong>：若广告包含效果对比或用户证言，需确保有真实数据支撑，且证言内容未涉及隐私泄露。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>落地页一致性</strong>：广告素材中的产品、服务描述需与落地页完全一致，不得存在夸大或隐藏信息。</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：<br />
- [ ] 文案无绝对化用语<br />
- [ ] 素材元素均有合法授权<br />
- [ ] 目标市场的年龄分级合规<br />
- [ ] 效果声称有数据支撑<br />
- [ ] 落地页与广告内容一致</p>
<hr />
<h2>环节三：落地页合规检查（3项检查）</h2>
<p>落地页是审核人员重点关注的对象，也是容易被忽视的合规盲区：</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>隐私政策链接</strong>：所有收集用户数据的落地页，必须在显著位置展示隐私政策链接，且隐私政策内容需符合GDPR、CCPA等法规要求。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>退订与退订机制</strong>：电商类落地页需提供清晰的退订、退款政策说明，且实际流程需与声明一致。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>联系方式公示</strong>：部分平台要求在落地页展示有效的联系方式（邮箱或地址），特别是金融、医疗类产品的广告落地页。</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：<br />
- [ ] 隐私政策链接可正常访问且内容完整<br />
- [ ] 退订退款政策清晰可见<br />
- [ ] 联系方式真实有效</p>
<hr />
<h2>环节四：数据与隐私合规（3项检查）</h2>
<p>数据合规是出海业务的高压线，一旦出问题可能面临巨额罚款：</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>像素与追踪工具</strong>：检查网站上部署的所有追踪像素（如Meta Pixel、TikTok Pixel）是否已获得用户的有效同意。欧盟及部分国家要求用户在Cookie Consent之后才能触发追踪。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>数据存储与跨境</strong>：确认用户数据的存储地点和跨境传输机制是否符合当地法规，特别是面向欧洲用户的业务需符合GDPR的数据本地化要求。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>再营销受众合规</strong>：使用历史用户数据进行再营销时，需确认这些用户当初是否已同意被用于营销目的。</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：<br />
- [ ] 追踪像素触发时机合规（需用户同意）<br />
- [ ] 数据存储与传输符合当地法规<br />
- [ ] 再营销受众有合法授权</p>
<hr />
<h2>环节五：账户与权限风控（3项检查）</h2>
<p>账户层面的风险往往影响整个投放体系：</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>账户权限分离</strong>：确保不同角色的账户权限设置合理，避免多人共用同一管理员账户，运营人员离职时及时移除权限。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>广告账户余额监控</strong>：设置账户余额预警，避免因余额不足导致投放中断。部分平台的账户欠费会影响信用记录。</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>支付方式合规性</strong>：确保广告账户绑定的支付方式（信用卡、对公账户、第三方支付平台）信息准确且在有效期内，支付方式过期是导致账户异常的原因之一。</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：<br />
- [ ] 账户权限与人员岗位匹配<br />
- [ ] 余额预警已设置且有效<br />
- [ ] 支付方式有效且信息准确</p>
<hr />
<h2>巡检后的跟进机制</h2>
<p>完成巡检后，负责人需要：</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>24小时内</strong>：修复发现的高风险问题（如被拒广告的共性问题）</li>
<li><strong>48小时内</strong>：更新内部合规文档，纳入新发现的风险点</li>
<li><strong>月度复盘</strong>：汇总当月违规数据，分析趋势并调整投放策略</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p>合规巡检不是一次性工作，而是需要持续执行的运营习惯。通过标准化的SOP，团队可以将合规风险从"被动应对"转变为"主动预防"。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Why Overseas Teams Need a Compliance Inspection SOP</h2>
<p>Overseas advertising platforms update their compliance policies frequently, and standards vary across channels like Facebook, TikTok, and Google. Policy violations often occur without clear notifications, and most teams only discover compliance issues after their accounts are suspended or ads are rejected—resulting in campaign interruptions and wasted budget.</p>
<p>An executable compliance inspection SOP enables teams to proactively identify risks before they escalate, rather than fighting fires reactively.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Pre-Inspection Setup: Define Responsibilities and Frequency</h2>
<p>Before conducting inspections, teams should establish these baseline settings:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Item</th>
<th>Recommended Practice</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Point Person</td>
<td>Assign 1 operator or risk control staff as inspection lead</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Frequency</td>
<td>Daily during high-risk periods (post-policy updates); weekly during stable periods</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Documentation</td>
<td>Use shared spreadsheets to record inspection results and follow-up status</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Module 1: Platform Policy Review (4 Checkpoints)</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>⚠️ This module is most frequently overlooked by teams.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Policy Update Tracking</strong>: Log into each ad platform's official policy page weekly to check for updates within the past 7 days. Facebook's "Policy Updates," TikTok's "Ads policies," and Google Ads' "Policy updates" all offer RSS or email subscription options.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Account Status Verification</strong>: Log into the ad dashboard and check all active accounts for health status indicators, confirming there are no unresolved policy violation warnings.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Ad Review History</strong>: Export ad review records from the past 14 days and flag all "rejected" or "restricted" ads. Analyze whether rejections share common causes.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>New Restricted Regions</strong>: When expanding into new markets, proactively check for special restrictions in target countries or regions—for example, some countries have strict requirements for financial product and health claim advertising.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Subscribed to policy update notifications across all platforms<br />
- [ ] No new policy violation warnings this week<br />
- [ ] Analyzed common reasons for rejected ads</p>
<hr />
<h2>Module 2: Creative Compliance Review (5 Checkpoints)</h2>
<p>Creatives are a high-risk area for violations. Review should occur both before launch and during routine inspections:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Claim Verification in Copy</strong>: Ad copy must not contain absolute statements (e.g., "best" or "100% effective") or unverified comparative claims. A utility app was once rejected by Facebook for using "fastest" in its copy.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Copyrights and Trademarks</strong>: All background music, fonts, and person imagery used in images and videos must be properly licensed. Use platform music libraries or commercially licensed tracks.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Age Rating and Content</strong>: Ensure creative content meets age classification requirements for target markets. European markets have strict age restriction labeling requirements for alcohol-related advertising.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Before/After Claims</strong>: If ads include effect comparisons or user testimonials, ensure they are backed by real data and that testimonials do not involve privacy breaches.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page Consistency</strong>: Product and service descriptions in ad creatives must exactly match the landing page—no embellishments or hidden information.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] No absolute language in copy<br />
- [ ] All creative elements are properly licensed<br />
- [ ] Age classification compliant for target market<br />
- [ ] Effect claims backed by data<br />
- [ ] Landing page matches ad content</p>
<hr />
<h2>Module 3: Landing Page Compliance (3 Checkpoints)</h2>
<p>Landing pages are a key focus for reviewers and often a blind spot for compliance:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Privacy Policy Link</strong>: All landing pages collecting user data must display a privacy policy link in a prominent position. Privacy policy content must comply with GDPR, CCPA, and other regulations.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Unsubscribe and Refund Mechanisms</strong>: E-commerce landing pages must provide clear refund and unsubscribe policy statements, and actual processes must match the stated terms.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Contact Information Display</strong>: Some platforms require valid contact information (email or address) on landing pages, particularly for financial and healthcare product advertising.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Privacy policy link accessible and complete<br />
- [ ] Refund/unsubscribe policies clearly visible<br />
- [ ] Contact information valid and current</p>
<hr />
<h2>Module 4: Data and Privacy Compliance (3 Checkpoints)</h2>
<p>Data compliance is a high-voltage area in overseas business—violations can result in massive fines:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Pixels and Tracking Tools</strong>: Verify that all tracking pixels deployed on websites (e.g., Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel) have valid user consent before triggering. The EU and some countries require users to consent to cookies before any tracking occurs.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Storage and Cross-Border Transfers</strong>: Confirm that user data storage locations and cross-border transfer mechanisms comply with local regulations, particularly GDPR data localization requirements for European users.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Remarketing Audience Compliance</strong>: When using historical user data for remarketing, verify that these users originally consented to being used for marketing purposes.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Tracking pixels trigger only after user consent<br />
- [ ] Data storage and transfer comply with local regulations<br />
- [ ] Remarketing audiences have valid authorization</p>
<hr />
<h2>Module 5: Account and Permission Risk Control (3 Checkpoints)</h2>
<p>Account-level risks often impact the entire advertising system:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Account Permission Separation</strong>: Ensure different roles have appropriate account permissions—avoid shared admin accounts. Remove permissions promptly when operators leave.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Ad Account Balance Monitoring</strong>: Set account balance alerts to avoid campaign interruptions due to insufficient funds. Some platforms affect credit records for unpaid balances.</p>
</li>
<li>
